      "file": "connection_pool.rs",
      "line": 903,
      "title": "Keyspace setup failures now log at DEBUG instead of WARN, losing visibility",
      "severity": "high",
      "kind": "bug",
      "claim": "Failed initialization USE requests previously logged at WARN and now log at DEBUG. When existing connections remain, the error also stays out of shared pool state. At INFO/WARN, repeated refill failures therefore become invisible to callers and operators.",
      "selfRejected": false
    },
    {
      "file": "connection_pool.rs",
      "line": 1634,
      "title": "New regression test has unbounded waits on keyspace request with no local timeout",
      "severity": "high",
      "kind": "test-gap",
      "claim": "Both new waits (lines 1634 and 1667) depend on a keyspace request without a local timeout. If that operation stalls, the test cannot reach its assertions or explicit proxy shutdown. Nextest supplies an external 120-second deadline, but the PR's documented cargo test invocation does not; the production timeout omission predates this PR.",
      "selfRejected": false
    },
    {
      "file": "connection_pool.rs",
      "line": 1474,
      "title": "New keyspace tests omit required tracing setup per CONTRIBUTING.md",
      "severity": "medium",
      "kind": "test-gap",
      "claim": "Neither new test (lines 1474 and 1526) calls setup_tracing(), despite CONTRIBUTING.md:92 directing new tests to do so. Isolated failures can consequently omit the required diagnostic tracing. The PR documents no exception.",
      "selfRejected": false
    }
